  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Contables** → se cuentan: *an apple, two apples, three carrots*. Tienen plural y admiten *a/an*, números y *many*.",
      "",
      "**Incontables** → no se cuentan: *milk, bread, rice, water, money, sugar, information, advice*. No tienen plural, no llevan *a/an* y van con *some / any / much*.",
      "",
      "**Ojo, son incontables en inglés:** *bread, information, advice, news, furniture, luggage, homework*. → *I need some advice.* (no *an advice*) · *The news is good.*",
      "",
      "**Cómo 'contar' lo incontable: envase + of**",
      "",
      "| Envase | Ejemplo |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a **bottle** of | water, olive oil, milk |",
      "| a **carton** of | juice, milk |",
      "| a **packet** of | rice, pasta, crisps |",
      "| a **tin / can** of | tomatoes, tuna |",
      "| a **jar** of | jam, honey |",
      "| a **loaf** of | bread |",
      "| a **slice** of | bread, cheese, pizza |",
      "| a **glass / cup** of | water / tea |",
      "",
      "Plural del envase: *two bottles of water, three loaves of bread*.",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *loaf* /ləʊf/ (plural *loaves* /ləʊvz/) · *onion* /ˈʌnjən/ · *vegetables* /ˈvedʒtəblz/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I need an advice.",
        "right": "I need some advice. / I need a piece of advice.",
        "note": "Advice es incontable."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "The news are good.",
        "right": "The news is good.",
        "note": "News es incontable y va con is."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
